    <string name="connection_address_help">For QuickConnect, enter only your QuickConnect ID.\n\nFor a direct connection, use the full address you use to open the NAS web interface, for example:\nhttps://192.168.1.10:5001\nhttp://192.168.1.10:5000\nUse the protocol and port configured on your NAS.\n\nAn IP address alone is treated as HTTPS without an explicit port. Windows file-sharing addresses are not supported.\n\nWith QuickConnect, you can also enter a local web address under Connection settings. The app tries that address first.\n\nThe connection indicator shows the method used for the successful sign-in; it does not monitor network availability.\n\nYou can add local, DDNS / remote and QuickConnect connections under More connection options. The app uses that priority order and skips the optional local connection on mobile data. Changing a connection address keeps your NAS profile, libraries and manual matches. Check connections tests each configured route without saving or consuming your verification code.</string>

